{{- /*
Files excluded from the target state, evaluated per host.

This is how a whole file disappears on a host that should not have it, rather
than rendering to something empty or commented out.

This file also doubles as the single choke point for validating the host slug.
It is rendered on every apply, so failing here fails the whole run with a
message that says what is actually wrong. Without it, an unknown slug surfaces
as `nil data; no entry for key "class"` from whichever template happened to be
rendered first, which says nothing useful about the real mistake.
*/ -}}
{{- if not (hasKey .hosts .hostID) -}}
{{-   fail (printf "unknown host slug %q — add it to home/.chezmoidata/hosts.toml, or correct hostID in this host's chezmoi config" .hostID) -}}
{{- end -}}
{{ if ne (index .hosts .hostID).class "macos" -}}
# Homebrew is macOS-only here. A Linux/WSL host gets no ~/.Brewfile at all.
.Brewfile
{{ end -}}
